  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Tin is obtained from cassiterite by reduction with coke. Use the data given below to determine the minimum temperature (in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>) at which the reduction of cassiterite by coke would take place.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>298</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#916;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></msub><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>SnO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>581</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#916;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></msub><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>394</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mfenced><mrow><msub><mo>SnO</mo><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>56</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>JK</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo>(</mo><mi>Sn</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>52</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>JK</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>JK</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>210</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>JK</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p>Assume that the enthalpies and the entropies are temperature independent.</p><p>&nbsp;</p>"
